From 8a9c23abe3b7d80b944d122c510c4e0528361841 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:08:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings: "HDR at more than 8 bits where the card sends RGB
 at 8 (NVIDIA)" is shown in the language of the user

The label and the help of videoscreen.hadeshdrmorebits (41011, 41012) were read from
the core's English strings in every language: GetLocalizedString() of the settings
dialog had no line for them, as it has for the other settings of Hades, which are read
from Estuary where the Spanish translations are. Their Estuary twins (32510, 32511), with
the same English and translated into es_es, es_ar and es_mx, were added in this version
and never read.

They are mapped like the others.

Host test (outside the tree): maptest.py parses GetLocalizedString() and checks that
every label, help and option of a setting of Hades (core ids from 39000) is mapped to an
Estuary string with the core's English and a translation in each Spanish file. Before,
these two are not mapped; after, they are (one other fault it finds, a stale msgid of
32911 in the Spanish files, has a commit of its own).
---
 xbmc/settings/dialogs/GUIDialogSettingsBase.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/settings/dialogs/GUIDialogSettingsBase.cpp b/xbmc/settings/dialogs/GUIDialogSettingsBase.cpp
index 38e7277..efedbd6 100644
--- a/xbmc/settings/dialogs/GUIDialogSettingsBase.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/settings/dialogs/GUIDialogSettingsBase.cpp
@@ -692,6 +692,9 @@ std::string CGUIDialogSettingsBase::GetLocalizedString(uint32_t labelId) const
   // the depth of HDR on the link (NVIDIA): label, help, values
   if (labelId >= 39873 && labelId <= 39876)
     return CGUIUtils::GetHadesString(labelId, 32114 + (labelId - 39873));
+  // HDR at more than 8 bits where the card sends RGB at 8 (NVIDIA): label, help
+  if (labelId == 41011 || labelId == 41012)
+    return CGUIUtils::GetHadesString(labelId, 32510 + (labelId - 41011));
   // native output, and Dolby Vision as HDR10 mapped to the display: labels, help, values
   if (labelId >= 39830 && labelId <= 39847)
     return CGUIUtils::GetHadesString(labelId, 31770 + (labelId - 39830));
